Z||000000||Ralfy9862||10-05-2001||09:07 AM||||i got my lowering springs on in march and have been told that my shocks and strutr were in need of being replaced. I have beeb driving the 87 gt fastback with bad shocks and stuts since then cause of no money to buy them im only 18(school full time). i was wondering if i damaged any of my suspension or if there are other things that i should replace when i get my kyb's put on in the spring like poly bushings or other things or should i look for anything specific that could be damaged. When i would go over bumps even little ones u could relly feel it and it sounded like my car is gonna fall apart........help please ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-05-2001||05:51 PM||||Hey Ralfy!<BR>Time to get a job...<BR>Save up your money and buy the replacement parts and have at it!<BR>I have done the suspentions on two Fieros now, and all of the problems were fixable...<BR>Upper and lower ball joints, shocks/struts, wheel bearings, bushings...<BR>Time consuming, but what a ride difference! Especially if you add the rear sway bar...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
